# AoC 2022 Day 5 — Channel multi-section demonstrator.
#
# The input has two structurally different sections (a crate drawing and a list
# of moves) that must both stay live and then combine. This program splits them
# into two Channels, processes each independently, and recombines with a From:
# consumer.
#
# It computes: (total crates moved across all moves) + (number of drawing rows).
# For the example input that is 7 + 4 = 11.
#
# NOTE: the full crate-rearrangement simulation (-> "CMZ") needs list/stack
# manipulation primitives inside lambda bodies, which are deferred past v0.2.
# This program exercises the Channel mechanism end-to-end on the real input.
Cursed Energy: input.txt
Cursed Technique: Split Text by "\n\n"

Channel "moves":
    Cursed Technique: Take Item 1
    Cursed Technique: Split Text by "\n"
    Cursed Technique: Match Pattern
        Using: "move {n:int} from {src:int} to {dst:int}"
    Cursed Technique: Map Each
        Using: (m) -> m.n
    Maximum Technique: Sum

Channel "rows":
    Cursed Technique: Take Item 0
    Cursed Technique: Split Text by "\n"
    Maximum Technique: Count

Maximum Technique: Combine
    From: moves, rows
    Using: (moves, rows) -> moves + rows

Reveal: stdout
